<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρής</span></b> , ὁ, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρητός</span>, mostly in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρῆτες, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span></span>,
			<u>Cretan</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.645
		</span></i>, etc.: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Κρὴς τὸν
		πόντον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγνοεῖ</span>), of
		those who feign ignorance, <i><span class="en">
			Alcm.
			115
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			10.4.17
		</span></i>:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρῆσσα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Sapph.
			54
		</span></i>: in pl., title of play by Aeschylus: as Adj.,
			<u>Cretan</u>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρῆτα τρόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρὴς ταῦρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.
					2.5.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητρὸς . . Κρήσσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					1295
				</span></i>
			:—regul. Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρήσιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				119
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				372
			</span></i> (both lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Limen.
				39
			</span></i>, etc.:—more freq. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span> (q.v.).</div>
